+### Phase 1: Setup
+
+- [ ] T001 Establish the delivery-status module and test locations, preserving the plan's single migration/service/controller shape
+
+**Implements**: FR-001 through FR-005
+
+**Pattern**: Inspect the application layout before implementation. Use the assumed locations below only if no established equivalent exists; update the affected task paths as one coherent change rather than mixing conventions.
+
+**Files**: `db/migrations/20260811000000_delivery_events.sql`, `src/reminders/`, `tests/integration/`
+
+### Phase 2: Tests First (TDD) — complete and observe failure before Phase 3
+
+- [ ] T002 [P] Write the failing provider-callback authentication integration test
+
+**Implements**: FR-001, FR-004
+
+**Scenario**: A validly signed callback reaches the idempotent service; a missing, altered, or invalid signature receives a rejection and writes no delivery event.
+
+**Pattern**: Exercise `POST /callbacks/reminder` through the request boundary, supplying the provider signature material exactly as the route will receive it. Do not mock away the verification boundary.
+
+**File**: `tests/integration/test_reminder_callback_auth.py`
+
+- [ ] T003 [P] Write the failing duplicate-delivery integration test
+
+**Implements**: FR-002, FR-003, FR-004
+
+**Scenario**: Send the same authenticated provider event twice and assert one workspace-scoped `delivery_events` record exists with the callback status; assert the duplicate response has no second persistence effect.
+
+**Pattern**: Run through `POST /callbacks/reminder` with the request role and inspect persisted rows, not only the HTTP response.
+
+**File**: `tests/integration/test_reminder_callback_idempotency.py`
+
+- [ ] T004 [P] Write the failing cross-workspace delivery-status integration test
+
+**Implements**: FR-005
+
+**Scenario**: A request-role principal in the owning workspace can read `GET /actions/{id}/delivery`; an otherwise valid principal from another workspace is denied and receives no delivery data.
+
+**Pattern**: Seed two workspaces and use real request-role context for both requests. A privileged service role is invalid evidence for this requirement.
+
+**File**: `tests/integration/test_action_delivery_workspace_scope.py`
+
+### Phase 3: Core Implementation — only after the three integration tests are failing
+
+- [ ] T005 Add the workspace-scoped, provider-event-unique delivery-event persistence schema
+
+**Implements**: FR-002, FR-003
+
+**Pattern**: Define `delivery_events` with workspace ID, action identity, provider event ID, and status. Encode uniqueness for the provider event at the database layer so concurrent callbacks cannot create duplicate records.
+
+**Security**: Retain workspace identity in the stored record and apply the repository's request-role/RLS convention if one is present; no cross-workspace lookup may rely on application filtering alone.
+
+**File**: `db/migrations/20260811000000_delivery_events.sql`
+
+- [ ] T006 Implement provider callback signature verification as a dedicated boundary helper
+
+**Implements**: FR-001
+
+**Pattern**: Accept the provider's raw callback material and signature data, return only a verification result or controlled failure, and keep provider-secret access out of persistence and query code.
+
+**Security**: Reject invalid or absent signatures before any delivery event is written; do not log provider secrets or raw credentials.
+
+**File**: `src/reminders/provider_signature.py`
+
+- [ ] T007 Implement the idempotent delivery callback service
+
+**Implements**: FR-002, FR-003
+
+**Pattern**: Accept verified callback data plus workspace/action context, persist the delivery status, and translate a duplicate provider event into the documented no-op outcome. Depend on the migration's uniqueness mechanism rather than a read-then-write race.
+
+**Testing**: Make the duplicate-delivery integration test pass without weakening its duplicate-row assertion.
+
+**File**: `src/reminders/delivery_events.py`
+
+- [ ] T008 Implement `POST /callbacks/reminder` with authenticate-before-persist ordering
+
+**Implements**: FR-001, FR-002, FR-003, FR-004
+
+**Pattern**: Route request material to `provider_signature.py`; on success call `delivery_events.py`; on failure return before invoking persistence. Preserve provider event ID and status through to the service.
+
+**Testing**: Make the authentication and duplicate-delivery integration tests pass through the actual route, including rejection with no persisted event.
+
+**File**: `src/reminders/callbacks.py`
+
+- [ ] T009 Implement workspace-scoped `GET /actions/{id}/delivery`
+
+**Implements**: FR-005
+
+**Pattern**: Resolve the authenticated request workspace first, then query delivery status using both workspace and action ID. Return the repository-standard missing/denied response without revealing another workspace's event.
+
+**Testing**: Make the cross-workspace integration test pass using the request role; do not substitute a service-role query.
+
+**File**: `src/reminders/delivery_status.py`
+
